  "caveats": [
    "One sequential combined-candidate live-city pair; profiling adds overhead. The route candidate was later reverted, so this pair does not measure the final retained configuration. No overall FPS, frame-tail or worst-frame improvement claim.",
    "Simulation timestamps and camera phase diverge slightly in real time: final tick55642 vs55639. Initial render draw counts also differ during transient scene/shadow work. Frozen-input compression and exact route comparisons isolate the demonstrated wins.",
    "The original midpoint diagnostic transferred full arrays and induced one roughly250ms gap; exclude that measurement artifact and startup gaps from frame-gap claims. The reusable harness transfers only a small midpoint summary.",
    "Foreground worker compression has similar/slightly longer wall completion time; the benefit is keeping the page responsive during compression. Hidden/unloading or unsupported/error cases preserve the existing page-thread fallback.",
    "Serialization and remaining route reskirting hitches are unresolved. This pass does not change snapshot timing or introduce asynchronous state serialization.",
    "The full Node suite remains affected by four observed failures with original routing code; the deferred candidate added an unresolved bridge-test failure. Browser save-store tests pass 11/11."
  ],
